  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "AP Chemistry",
      "left": 1205.3,
      "top": 39.21333333333334,
      "width": 154.9011666666666,
      "height": 36.635000000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "Use these answers for questions 7-10",
      "left": 85,
      "top": 80.31593333333333,
      "width": 509.6481,
      "height": 45.34920000000001
    },
    {
      "text": "(A) Heisenberg uncertainty principle (B) Pauli exclusion principle",
      "left": 169.9966,
      "top": 117.77543333333334,
      "width": 867.37638,
      "height": 42.862949999999984
    },
    {
      "text": "(D) Shielding effect",
      "left": 169.9966,
      "top": 155.16863333333333,
      "width": 251.40960000000004,
      "height": 42.86295000000001
    },
    {
      "text": "(E) Wave nature of matter",
      "left": 486.840985,
      "top": 155.16863333333333,
      "width": 338.04049499999996,
      "height": 42.86295000000001
    },
    {
      "text": "(C) Hund's rule",
      "left": 1094.98768,
      "top": 117.77543333333334,
      "width": 198.54198,
      "height": 42.862949999999984
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Can be used to predict that a gaseous carbon atom in its ground state is paramagnetic",
      "left": 127.4983,
      "top": 229.42463333333333,
      "width": 1133.9487900000001,
      "height": 42.862949999999984
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Explains the experimental phenomenon of electron diffraction",
      "left": 127.4983,
      "top": 266.55263333333335,
      "width": 845.1493049999999,
      "height": 42.86295000000001
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Indicates that an atomic orbital can hold no more than two electrons",
      "left": 127.4983,
      "top": 303.9458333333333,
      "width": 921.997635,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Predicts that it is impossible to determine simultaneously the exact position and the exact",
      "left": 127.4983,
      "top": 341.07383333333337,
      "width": 1183.39533,
      "height": 42.862949999999984
    },
    {
      "text": "velocity of an electron",
      "left": 169.9966,
      "top": 378.20183333333335,
      "width": 284.735295,
      "height": 42.862949999999984
    },
    {
      "text": "11. The elements I and Te have similar average atomic masses. A sample that was believed to",
      "left": 127.4983,
      "top": 601.5002333333333,
      "width": 1211.284425,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "be a mixture of I and Te was run through a mass spectrometer, resulting in the data below.",
      "left": 169.9966,
      "top": 638.6282333333334,
      "width": 1160.8301250000002,
      "height": 42.86294999999991
    },
    {
      "text": "All of the following statements are true. Which one would be the best basis for concluding",
      "left": 170.02975,
      "top": 1058.2409333333333,
      "width": 1166.4623099999997,
      "height": 42.86294999999991
    },
    {
      "text": "that the sample was pure Te?",
      "left": 170.02975,
      "top": 1095.3689333333332,
      "width": 372.251295,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "a. Te forms ions with a -2 charge, whereas I forms ions with a -1 charge",
      "left": 212.52805,
      "top": 1132.7621333333334,
      "width": 931.26969,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "b. Te is more abundant than I in the universe.",
      "left": 212.52805,
      "top": 1169.8901333333333,
      "width": 596.66022,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "c. I consists of only one naturally occurring isotope with 74 neutrons, whereas Te has",
      "left": 212.52805,
      "top": 1207.0181333333333,
      "width": 1105.065195,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "more than one isotope",
      "left": 255.02635,
      "top": 1244.1461333333334,
      "width": 290.10227999999995,
      "height": 42.862949999999785
    },
    {
      "text": "d. I has a higher first ionization energy than Te does",
      "left": 212.52805,
      "top": 1281.5393333333332,
      "width": 678.0070049999999,
      "height": 42.86295000000005
    },
    {
      "text": "27",
      "left": 708.3333333333334,
      "top": 1801.7166666666667,
      "width": 28.333333333333332,
      "height": 38.16499999999997
    }
  ]
}
